# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Web app (Vite) environment template.
# Copy to `apps/web/.env` ONLY if you need to override the repo-root `.env`.
# Everything here is local-development configuration, never a secret: Vite
# inlines any VITE_-prefixed value into the client bundle, so no credential,
# token, key or password may ever be put in this file.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# Origin the dev server forwards /api/* to. Resolution order:
#   1. this variable (process env or .env file)
#   2. API_PORT from the repo-root .env  →  http://127.0.0.1:<API_PORT>
#   3. built-in default                  →  http://127.0.0.1:3000
# An invalid value fails the dev server at startup instead of silently
# proxying somewhere wrong (see apps/web/proxy-target.ts).
#
# 127.0.0.1, not localhost: localhost resolves to BOTH ::1 and 127.0.0.1, so a
# refused connection is reported as `AggregateError [ECONNREFUSED]` naming
# neither address.
#
# Build output is unaffected — production requests go to /api/v1 on the SPA's
# own origin and are routed by the reverse proxy in front of it.
VITE_API_PROXY_TARGET=http://127.0.0.1:3000
